  "question": {
    "text": "A conducting bubble of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;has potential <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math>. Now, the bubble collapses into a droplet. The potential of the droplet is"
  },
  "options": [
